  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Sanctioned Psyker" id="330d-1cf9-e3cd-b4b6" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="12"/>
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Sanctioned Psyker" id="6804-f0ef-8ea1-4f05" hidden="false" targetId="362e-f73d-1b3f-7727" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Laspistol" id="8e0c-3375-5b4b-df04" hidden="false" targetId="95a9-d270-d218-1772" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Close Combat Weapon" id="d210-d914-e7c6-481a" hidden="false" targetId="46d5-85f2-d932-f0a2" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Lightning Arc" id="5d07-db50-bca3-cc1f" hidden="false" targetId="10fd-f6eb-b85c-960f" type="profile"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Psychic Powers" id="77c4-9fdb-7118-1c29" hidden="false">
          <description>Roll for one power selected at random at the start of the game:
1 - No useable power
2 - Telepathic Order
3 - Psychic Ward
4 - Lightning Arc
5 - Psychic Lash
6 - Machine Curse</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="It&apos;s For Your Own Good!" id="7a76-115a-51be-a069" hidden="false">
          <description>If a Commissar is attached to the same unit as the psyker, and they suffer a Perils of the Warp attack, the Commissar will immediately execute him to prevent him from being possessed. Remove the Psyker model as a casualty. The power he was attempting to use does not work.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Telepathic Order" id="c470-3a69-6124-774d" hidden="false">
          <description>The Psyker extends the zone of influence of an Officer he is accompanying. Use at the start of the Imperial Guard turn. If the test is passed, the Leadership radius of the Officer in the same squad as the Psyker is extended to 18&quot; until the start of the next Imperial Guard turn.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Psychic Ward" id="4ad4-0f82-807f-b2a4" hidden="false">
          <description>If a psychic power would normally affect the Sanctioned Psyker or the unit he is accompanying, make a Psychic test. If the test is passed then roll a D6. On a 4+ the power is cancelled.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Psychic Lash" id="daad-7363-bb0c-1107" hidden="false">
          <description>Make a Psychic test at the start of the Imperial Guard Assault phase. If successful, the power remains in phase until the start of the next Imperial Guard Assault phase. The Psyker&apos;s may choose to use the Lash in place of its normal attacks. The Psyker gets D3 Attacks (with no bonuses) at Strength 3, with any wounds ignoring Armour saves.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Machine Curse" id="dcce-7283-ce71-2117" hidden="false">
          <description>Make the Psychic test at the start of the Assault phase. If passed the power is effective until the end of the same Assault phase. Make one close combat attack against a vehicle in base contact with the Psyker. If a hit is scored, roll a D6:
1 - 3: No effect
4 - 5: Inflict Glancing Hit
6 : Inflict Penetrating Hit</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
